# launch-mind-cardinal-chapter.rish -- print the loop for MIND, the cardinal star of the aether row.
#
# Mind (night twin Mystery) is CHATGPT ON MACOS -- the Arbor session in the ChatGPT desktop app,
# aether at the cardinal seat, the word that initiates: the star that opens the surfaces a
# person touches. Its lane: Brushstroke and Surf (elder code name Skate) for macOS, with
# everything in the DJINN design lead staying custody gate %6. Charter:
# active-designing/20260826-151528_the-three-stars-of-the-aether-row.md. The Arbor session
# speaks in tiles rather than a shell loop, so its living loop is the spoken Brix at
# arbor/launch-chatgpt-chapter.brix, rendered and verified by arbor/author.sh -- this script
# carries the elder recipe's shape (preconditions, the spoken flow, the seat, custody) the way
# tools/l/launch-claude-chapter.rish does for a shell bench. Siblings:
# launch-sound-fixed-chapter.rish (Claude Code, macOS) - launch-dream-dual-chapter.rish (Claude
# Code in ai-jail, the Vultr pier).
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/l/launch-mind-cardinal-chapter.rish

# invariant: run from the repo root, where the durable memory lives.
let root = run ["test" "-f" "construction/ITINERARY.md"]
assert root.ok else "run from the repo root (construction/ITINERARY.md not found)"

# invariant: the spoken loop this recipe points at must exist.
let brix = run ["test" "-f" "arbor/launch-chatgpt-chapter.brix"]
assert brix.ok else "arbor/launch-chatgpt-chapter.brix (the spoken loop) is missing"

say "MIND -- the cardinal star of the aether row (night twin Mystery)"
say "================================================================"
say ""
say "Host: CHATGPT ON MACOS -- the Arbor session in the desktop app. Its loop is"
say "spoken rather than shelled: the Lattice tiles in"
say "arbor/launch-chatgpt-chapter.brix, rendered and verified by arbor/author.sh,"
say "name this seat. The shared discipline lives on the living card either way."
say ""
say "0) PRECONDITIONS, once per machine: the ChatGPT desktop app signed in on the"
say "   Mac; this repo cloned where the session can read it; the tiles current --"
say "   render and verify them with:  sh arbor/author.sh"
say ""
say "1) THE SPOKEN FLOW: read the rendered tiles aloud into the Arbor session, or"
say "   paste them -- each tile is at or under the 256-byte tile bound and carries"
say "   no digits, per Lattice's own rules. The tiles point the session at the"
say "   living card and the charter, so a directive seated there reaches the next"
say "   spoken lap with no tile edit."
say ""
say "2) THE SEAT, for a hand that wants it in one line:"
say ""
say "You are MIND, the cardinal star of the aether row, night twin Mystery, in the Arbor session on macOS: your lane is Brushstroke and Surf (elder code name Skate) for macOS, and everything in the DJINN design lead stays custody gate %6. Caravan, Tally, and the Scribe seams belong to Sound (fixed, Claude Desktop); the Glow rune lowering to Dream (dual, the pier); a find in a sibling lane becomes a line in ITINERARY rather than your lap. The remote is named xy on this clone; the seed cadence rides with Dream alone. STOP at the custody gates in ITINERARY. ty every1 baton prin recur"
say ""
say "3) CUSTODY: the gates in ITINERARY stay MANUAL -- and everything in the"
say "   DJINN design lead stays custody gate %6, the invitation and every seat in"
say "   that domain the collaborator's to accept. A find in a sibling lane"
say "   becomes a line on the card rather than this star's lap."
say ""
say "GREEN: Mind recipe printed -- the cardinal star opens what a person touches."
